## Report
Validated. Dynamic PoC test was injected and run against the real Rust HttpFrontend path. The test creates `existing-bucket`, installs a failing identity provider to prove authentication is not consulted, and sends unauthenticated S3 Control OPTIONS requests with Origin and Access-Control-Request-Method headers through `handle_service_request(EndpointKind::SharedRegional, ...)`. Command: `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 RUSTFLAGS='-C debuginfo=1' cargo test -p server-http poc_unauthenticated_s3_control_options_distinguishes_bucket_existence -- --nocapture`. Output showed missing bucket: `status=403 ... <Code>AccessForbidden</Code><Message>CORSResponse: Bucket not found</Message>...`; existing bucket: `status=403 ... <Code>AccessDenied</Code><Message>Access Denied</Message>...`. This confirms a distinguishable unauthenticated bucket-existence oracle. Code evidence: `crates/server-http/src/http/router.rs:494-500` routes S3 Control `OPTIONS` to `S3ControlOperation::Options { bucket }`; `crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs:1025-1045` handles S3 and S3 Control OPTIONS before the SigV4 authentication block at `mod.rs:1098-1107`; `mod.rs:1277-1290` checks Origin/ACRM then calls `bucket_exists_on_admitted_route` and returns different responses for `Ok(false)` and `Ok(true)`; `crates/server-core/src/coordinator/bucket.rs:529-532` performs `unchecked_active_bucket_summary_for_admitted_route` and converts existence to bool; `crates/server-http/src/http/response.rs:2395-2405` builds the distinct missing-bucket `AccessForbidden` / `CORSResponse: Bucket not found` response. LLDB breakpoint at `bucket.rs:529` produced stack: `Coordinator::bucket_exists_on_admitted_route` -> `HttpFrontend::handle_s3_control_options` at `mod.rs:1286` -> `HttpFrontend::handle_service_request` at `mod.rs:1040` -> PoC test, confirming the unauthenticated OPTIONS path reaches the unchecked existence lookup. Direct crash was attempted via the PoC test but this is a logic/info-disclosure flaw and no crash is expected. Valgrind was unavailable (`bash: command not found: valgrind`); ASan build attempt failed because `-Z sanitizer=address` requires nightly Rust.

